#!/usr/bin/python3
"""The workspace image job, run as root by portikus-image-job.service.

It takes the request files the API writes into the job directory and runs
one fixed job per request: fetch, build, activate or rollback
(docs/SPEC.md section 22.4, ADR 0030). The file contract is the
comment at the top of packages/contracts/src/image.ts.

Python rather than shell: strict JSON validation, atomic writes through
directory file descriptors, a lock and argument-list subprocesses are all
plain here and error-prone in shell. python3 is on every host through
ansible-core; only the standard library is used (PyYAML, which ansible-core
depends on, is imported only to read /etc/portikus/portikus.yaml).

Usage:
  image-job                 take and run pending requests (the unit)
  image-job recover         mark a job the host lost as failed (ExecStopPost)
  image-job first-install VERSION
                            setup's first install: fetch VERSION and make it
                            the default, unless the host has a default already
  image-job check           write images/published.json: the newest published
                            image and any newer portikus package (the daily timer)
  image-job local-build     build the shipped recipe and make it the default
                            (make build-workspace-image on a development VM)
  image-job manifest ...    print a schema 1 manifest for a built rootfs
                            (also used by .github/workflows/workspace-image.yml)
"""

